
This directory contains PlatformIO host/native tests for firmware logic that
does not require ESP32 hardware.

Project-specific layout:

- `test_detector_baseline/`: angular/default/confidence regressions;
- `test_fall_detector_replay/`: deterministic synthetic FSM sequences;
- `support/`: reusable replay and `SensorReading` builders;
- `native_stubs/`: minimal test-only Arduino surface needed to compile the
  real `FallDetector` on the host.

The replay input boundary is `std::vector<SensorReading>`. A future CSV/JSON
parser can remain separate and produce this same input without changing the
harness. Current sequences are synthetic and do not represent physical or
clinical validation.

Run with:

```text
platformio test -e native
```

This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
